Subject: [PATCH] net: ena: give up resume when the device is gone

A hibernation image restored on another machine resumes with no ENA
device behind the old BAR. Every admin command then times out against
all-ones reads and pci_pm_restore loops forever. Detach and leave it down.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/amazon/ena/ena_netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/amazon/ena/ena_netdev.c
@@ -4259,6 +4259,12 @@
 	struct ena_adapter *adapter = dev_get_drvdata(dev_d);
 	int rc;
 
+	if (!pci_device_is_present(to_pci_dev(dev_d))) {
+		dev_warn(dev_d, "Device gone after resume\n");
+		netif_device_detach(adapter->netdev);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	ena_increase_stat(&adapter->dev_stats.resume, 1, &adapter->syncp);
 
 	rtnl_lock();
